From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Build tooling contributors <build-tools@example.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:14:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: distinguish analysis from completed builds

Analysis metadata can be mistaken for successful build outcomes, while
repeated final updates can replace target results and diagnostic logs.

Retain analysis metadata and finalize actual outcomes once. Preserve late
client records when supplied and close ended streams through the existing
quiet-period and shutdown boundaries when no final record arrives.

As Bazel does, report target events only for the targets a build, test or
install command requested, those its ParsedTargetPatterns match; announce a
dependency's action events with the next progress event. A requested target
whose analysis declares no actions completes when the command finishes, and
one that a successful command did not build closes as Aborted, SKIPPED. A
failed command closes neither.
---
